## Project Overview
Developed a machine learning-based system to forecast 5G network traffic and identify Quality of Service (QoS) anomalies using network performance data.

## Objectives
- Forecast network traffic 24 hours ahead.
- Detect abnormal network behavior.
- Support proactive congestion management and network reliability.

## Technologies Used
Python, Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-learn, XGBoost, Isolation Forest, Matplotlib, Seaborn.

## Dataset
- 504 hourly records
- 3 base stations
- Network metrics including traffic volume, latency, packet loss, throughput, and signal quality.

## Model Evaluation
- Traffic forecasting: MAE = 1.762 GB/hour
- Traffic forecasting: RMSE = 2.229 GB/hour
- Anomaly detection: 2 of 3 known anomalies detected (66.7%)

